    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 2</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 2</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 50%;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Reading</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Sustainable Fashion</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How History Is Fashionable</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Reading: Derive the meaning of simple unknown words from short texts. Reading: Summarize narratives of significant events, recent or historical.</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Reading: Can infer the meaning of unknown words in a fashion trend article by using context clues and comparing terms (e.g., "The word 'vintage' in this article refers to old-fashioned clothing styles that were popular in previous decades.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can summarize main points in a text about past fashion trends (e.g., "Describe two major styles from a fashion trends article, such as shoulder pads and bold colors from the 1980s." "Identify key features of 1990s streetwear, like baggy jeans and graphic t-shirts.")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Can determine the meaning of new terms in a piece about eco-friendly materials (e.g., "Tagua is an example of eco-friendly material. It is the seed of a tree that can be used to make jewelry.").</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays a collage of images showing various fashion trends from different historical periods (e.g., 1980s shoulder pads, 1990s grunge, 2000s low-rise jeans) alongside images of current sustainable fashion (e.g., upcycled clothing, eco-friendly materials like bamboo or organic cotton). Students, in pairs, briefly discuss what they notice about the styles and materials. The teacher asks, "Which styles look 'vintage' or 'retro'?" and "Do you see any 'sustainable' or 'eco-friendly' materials?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models reading a short sentence related to the images, focusing on the pronunciation of /v/ in "vintage" and /w/ in "wear," and stressing "fashionable" and "sustainability." For example, "Many designers are creating new collections inspired by <b>vintage</b> styles." and "People today <b>wear</b> clothes that reflect a growing interest in <b>sustainability</b>."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If something is 'vintage,' is it brand new or from the past?" (Expected answer: From the past.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Does 'eco-friendly' mean it's good for the environment or bad for it?" (Expected answer: Good for the environment.)</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 2 — Presentation</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> A B1.1 level short article titled "From Bell Bottoms to Bamboo: How Fashion Has Evolved Towards Sustainability," excerpted from a fictional online fashion blog. The text includes various paragraphs describing past fashion trends (e.g., "In the 1970s, people were wearing bell-bottoms. Today, flared jeans are in style.") and discusses the shift towards eco-friendly materials and sustainable brands. It contains target grammar (past continuous, past perfect, future simple) and vocabulary (fashion, trend, vintage, retro, materials, sustainability, designs, environment, evolve, adopt, reflect, recycle, eco-friendly).</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Reading: Derive the meaning of simple unknown words from short texts.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students read the article silently.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Gist Question:</b> "What is the main idea of this article?" (Students choose from multiple-choice options, e.g., a) The history of music, b) How fashion has changed over time and become more sustainable, c) The cost of clothes).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>True/False Statements:</b> Students read specific statements and decide if they are true or false according to the article (e.g., "In the 1980s, people were wearing minimalistic designs." "The article predicts that fashion trends will continue to evolve towards sustainability.").</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Reading.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Grammar:</b> Past continuous with present simple to compare trends; Past perfect for completed actions; Future simple for predictions.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Vocabulary:</b> fashion, trend, vintage, retro, collection, style, materials, sustainability, launch, show, industry, brands, designs, runway, environment, prediction, history, personality, future, evolve, predict, launch, adopt, reflect, discuss, shop, design, notice, gain, create, follow, introduce, showcase, wear, prefer, inspire, change, return, recycle, sustainable, fashionable, trendy, eco-friendly, vintage, retro, stylish, innovative, unique, recycled.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pronunciation:</b> Practice /v/ in "vintage" and /w/ in "wear." Stress in "fashionable," "sustainability," "eco-friendly," "runway."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pragmatic:</b> Asking about fashion trends; Discussing eco-friendly fashion choices.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">1. <b>Inferring Meaning from Context:</b> Students receive a worksheet with 5-7 sentences directly from the article containing target vocabulary words (e.g., "vintage," "eco-friendly," "sustainability," "evolve," "adopt"). Below each sentence, they are given two possible definitions for the underlined word. Students must choose the best definition based on the context of the sentence. Teacher checks answers, providing explanation. (Focus: Reading: Derive the meaning of simple unknown words.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">2. <b>Timeline Reading & Sentence Completion:</b> Students re-read specific paragraphs of the article to identify historical fashion trends. They complete a timeline graphic organizer with sentences extracted from the text, using past continuous for ongoing trends (e.g., "In the 1980s, people were wearing bold colors and big shoulder pads.") and past perfect for actions completed before another past action (e.g., "By the 2000s, people had adopted more casual fashion styles."). They then write one prediction about future fashion using future simple (e.g., "Fashion brands will introduce more recycled materials.").</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">3. <b>Pair Trend Comparison:</b> In pairs, students discuss specific fashion trends from different decades mentioned in the article. They take turns asking and answering questions like, "How have fashion trends evolved from the 1970s to today?" and "What were people wearing in the 1990s, and what are people wearing today that reflects those styles?" They must summarize at least two major styles from a specific decade from the article (e.g., "The article describes the 1980s with shoulder pads and bold colors."). Teacher circulates, monitoring use of grammar and pronunciation.</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Sustainable Fashion".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Summary & Discussion.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Activity:</b> Students work in small groups (3-4 students). Each group is assigned a different section of the "How Fashion Has Evolved" article (e.g., "Historical Trends," "Modern Fashion & Sustainability," "The Future of Fashion"). Each group reads their section again and prepares a 1-minute oral summary, using specific vocabulary (e.g., 'vintage,' 'retro,' 'eco-friendly,' 'sustainable,' 'evolve') and the target grammar (past continuous/present simple, past perfect, future simple). They also identify key features of styles and eco-friendly materials mentioned in their section (e.g., "Tagua is an example of an eco-friendly material; it's a seed used for jewelry."). After each group presents their summary, a brief class discussion is held. The teacher prompts with questions like, "What had people adopted before the rise of sustainable brands?" and "How will fashion continue to evolve in the future?" encouraging students to discuss eco-friendly fashion choices (e.g., "By using eco-friendly fabrics, fashion brands can reduce their carbon footprint, helping to protect the environment."). This allows for students to showcase how language reflects people's values regarding sustainability.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</b></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher observation checklist during group discussions and a short written task.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students will write a short paragraph (50-70 words) summarizing one significant historical fashion trend described in the article, ensuring they include at least two specific features. Additionally, they must identify two unknown words from the text (other than those practiced in Stage 3), infer their meaning using context clues, and briefly explain their reasoning (e.g., "The word 'textile' in the article means 'fabric' because it was used in the sentence about different materials for clothing.").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and accuracy of the summary of the historical fashion trend.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Ability to infer the meaning of unknown words using context clues.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., 'vintage,' 'trend,' 'style') and past tenses (past continuous, past perfect).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Sentence structure and overall comprehensibility.</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was the most interesting historical fashion trend you read about today, and why?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Name one strategy you used today to figure out the meaning of a new word in the article."</li>
                </ul>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>STAGE 6 — Reflection</b></p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What did you learn about sustainable fashion from reading the article today?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did identifying past fashion trends help you understand the current movement towards sustainability?"</li>
                </ul>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b> What strategies for deriving meaning from context worked well? Were students able to summarize narratives effectively? Did the article's language level (B1.1) align with student comprehension? Were the pronunciation points (/v/, /w/, word stress) naturally integrated? What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for students struggling with vocabulary or complex sentences in future reading tasks?</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> In the next lesson (Speaking & Interaction), students will use the knowledge gained from today's reading to discuss their opinions on historical fashion trends and the importance of sustainable choices, practicing asking and answering questions about fashion's evolution and making predictions about its future.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">2-3 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>